# The library hand (#467.1): the WebXR generic hand (MIT, data/core/vr/hands/webxr/) as the arms model `library`:
# cfg vr_arms_model = custom | arx | library, the channel command `arms library`, status.json vr.body.armsModel.
# PROPOSED status field: vr.body.<hand>.library.drawn (true while that hand's library mesh is drawn; a new field
# rather than the glove's custom.gloveDrawn, which stays false for any hand but the glove). The held weapon's
# hilt pose and its curl on the handle are the glove's own fields (vr.hands.<hand>.hiltPose,
# vr.body.<hand>.custom.curlToHandle), which the library hand must fill too.
# Needs the first-person save with the sword equipped:
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 arms-library
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence arms-library -Save mvp-items
@sim idle
@save mvp-items
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.body.bound eq true
@assert vr.body.active eq true

vr-sim head rot 0 -40 0
vr-sim hand left off
vr-sim hand right pos 0.12 -0.1 -0.35
vr-sim hand right rot 0 90 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@shot model-before

# 1. The library hand: the model is set and the right hand's mesh is drawn
arms library
@frames 10
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq library
@assert vr.body.right.library.drawn eq true
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.right.error lt 1
@shot model-library

# 2. The sword in the right hand: a hilt pose is in use and the curl lies on the handle
@assert vr.body.right.fingers.holds eq true
@assert vr.hands.right.hiltPose ne none
@assert vr.body.right.custom.curlToHandle lt 0.5
@shot library-sword

# 3. Back to the custom glove: the library hand is no longer drawn
arms custom
@frames 10
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq custom
@assert vr.body.right.library.drawn eq false
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@shot model-custom-again

@assert errors eq 0
